meta {
  name: Get Chart Defaults
  type: http
  seq: 23
}

get {
  url: {{protocol}}://{{host}}:{{port}}/{{apiPrefix}}analytes/{{temperatureAnalyteId}}/chart-defaults
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

script:pre-request {
  if (!bru.getVar('temperatureAnalyteId')) {
    await bru.runRequest("analytes/list-vitals");
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Which dose markers this metric's chart shows **by default** (api.md → "Chart overlay defaults";
  data-model.md → `ChartOverlayDefault`).

  Display config, not a recorded relationship: a row means "show antipyretic doses on the
  temperature chart unless the reader filters otherwise", never "antipyretics affect temperature".
  The app is saying *you probably want these visible together* and nothing more — the chart's
  no-annotation rule is unchanged, and no computed "responsive to X" text ever renders on a marker.

  Household-global like the analyte catalog itself: authenticated, no patient scoping. Works
  identically on a seeded vital and on a lab analyte, since a vital *is* an analyte row.

  Out of the box `yarn seed:catalog` seeds two: antipyretic doses on the `temperature` chart, and
  analgesic doses on the `pain_score` chart. Nothing re-seeds them, so a delete sticks.

  404 `ANALYTE_NOT_FOUND` on an unknown id.
}
